WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.279 --> 00:00:02.560
(upbeat music)

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:04.018
- [Karmele] The difference
between orangutans

00:00:04.018 --> 00:00:05.432
and other animals,

00:00:05.432 --> 00:00:08.349
they need this process of learning.

00:00:09.541 --> 00:00:11.740
They learn by imitating.

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:13.740
They learn by observing.

00:00:15.701 --> 00:00:18.920
So that's why we created
these forest schools,

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:21.312
where they can learn from each other.

00:00:21.312 --> 00:00:23.812
(happy music)

00:00:26.709 --> 00:00:30.594
This is the International
Animal Rescue Center

00:00:30.594 --> 00:00:32.844
for orangutans in Ketapang.

00:00:33.815 --> 00:00:36.065
We have now 102 orangutans.

00:00:37.632 --> 00:00:41.036
We come across orangutans that are

00:00:41.036 --> 00:00:42.975
kept as pets illegally.

00:00:42.975 --> 00:00:46.476
We also rescue them for the
habitat that is disappearing.

00:00:46.476 --> 00:00:47.844
When we rescue orangutans,

00:00:47.844 --> 00:00:50.106
especially when they are small babies,

00:00:50.106 --> 00:00:52.815
these babies have lost their mothers.

00:00:52.815 --> 00:00:55.124
Normally an orangutan will remain

00:00:55.124 --> 00:00:57.316
with its mother for as long as

00:00:57.316 --> 00:01:00.135
seven to eight years of their lives.

00:01:00.135 --> 00:01:04.026
And this is the process when
the orangutans have the chance

00:01:04.026 --> 00:01:07.546
to learn from their mothers
how to survive in the wild,

00:01:07.546 --> 00:01:08.706
what to eat,

00:01:08.706 --> 00:01:10.208
what not to eat,

00:01:10.208 --> 00:01:12.524
what are the dangers of the forest.

00:01:12.524 --> 00:01:14.444
What we have to do is to teach them

00:01:14.444 --> 00:01:16.694
how to survive in the wild.

00:01:18.221 --> 00:01:20.804
(joyful music)

00:01:21.879 --> 00:01:23.359
In these forest schools,

00:01:23.359 --> 00:01:26.618
one of the first ones is
how to be off the ground,

00:01:26.618 --> 00:01:29.658
how to spend time on the top of the trees.

00:01:29.658 --> 00:01:32.800
Which, it might seem like a very simple thing,

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:34.448
but actually some of these orangutans

00:01:34.448 --> 00:01:35.910
are having living with people

00:01:35.910 --> 00:01:39.510
and having chained up or
living in small cages.

00:01:39.510 --> 00:01:42.709
At the beginning they are
afraid to climb a tree.

00:01:42.709 --> 00:01:45.539
The ultimate goal of this rehabilitation

00:01:45.539 --> 00:01:48.800
is to release these
animals back to the wild.

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:50.659
What is special with orangutans

00:01:50.659 --> 00:01:53.590
is they are very similar to humans.

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:56.423
If we don't care about orangutans,

00:01:57.808 --> 00:01:59.880
I think it's even more difficult

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:03.470
that we are going to care
about any of the other species.

00:02:03.470 --> 00:02:05.400
If they get extinct in Indonesia

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:08.599
they will be extinct from
the face of the world.

00:02:08.599 --> 00:02:11.699
So we have to do something about this now.

00:02:11.699 --> 00:02:14.282
(joyful music)

